TOOL_CALL: ap_research_pieces {"pieceNames":"[\"linkedin\"]","forIntent":"post to LinkedIn on a schedule every morning"}
TOOL_RESULT: null
ASSISTANT: Love this idea — a daily LinkedIn post is a great way to stay visible and build your audience. Before I wire up the automation, I need to settle one key thing: **what should it actually post each morning?**
TOOL_CALL: ap_show_questions {"questions":[{"type":"choice","title":"Daily post content","question":"What should the automation post to LinkedIn each morning?","options":[{"label":"AI-generated post on a topic I choose","icon":"sparkles","description":"You pick a theme/niche; AI writes a fresh, unique post every day"},{"label":"Pull from a content queue","icon":"table","description":"You prepare posts in advance in a spreadsheet or table; it publishes one per day"},{"label":"Summarize something (news, blog, RSS)","icon":"globe","description":"Auto-summarize an article, RSS feed, or newsletter and turn it into a LinkedIn post"},{"label":"Fixed rotating posts","icon":"repeat","description":"Cycle through a fixed list of posts you've already written"}]}]}
TOOL_RESULT: {"dismissed":true,"message":"The user skipped these questions. Proceed with reasonable defaults where possible, and let the user know what assumptions you made."}
ASSISTANT: I'll go with AI-generated posts — that's the most hands-off and keeps content fresh daily. Let me get everything set up.
TOOL_CALL: ap_select_project {"projectId":"eval-project"}
TOOL_RESULT: null
TOOL_CALL: ap_show_questions {"questions":[{"type":"choice","title":"Post topic / niche","question":"What should the AI write about each morning?","options":[{"label":"My industry & professional insights","icon":"briefcase"},{"label":"Leadership & productivity tips","icon":"sparkles"},{"label":"Tech & innovation trends","icon":"zap"},{"label":"Motivational & mindset content","icon":"sun"},{"label":"Custom topic I'll describe","icon":"pencil"}]}]}
TOOL_RESULT: {"dismissed":true,"message":"The user skipped these questions. Proceed with reasonable defaults where possible, and let the user know what assumptions you made."}
ASSISTANT: Got it — I'll move forward with sensible defaults and we can tune the content angle after it's built.

Here's the plan: every morning at 8 AM, AI generates a professional LinkedIn post (I'll default to professional insights & tips), and it gets published to your LinkedIn profile automatically.

Let me start by connecting your LinkedIn account.
TOOL_CALL: ap_show_connection_picker {"piece":"linkedin","displayName":"LinkedIn"}
TOOL_RESULT: {"dismissed":true,"message":"The user chose not to select a LinkedIn account. Do not pick one on their behalf. Ask: \"Would you like me to continue building with a placeholder you can connect later, or would you prefer to stop here?\""}
